// Title: Gzip Archive Decode Via PowerShell
// Sigma ID: 98767d61-b2e8-4d71-b661-e36783ee24c1
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Hieu Tran
// Date: 2023-03-13 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1132.001
// Description: Detects attempts of decoding encoded Gzip archives via PowerShell.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative scripts may use this functionality. Use "ParentImage" in combination with the script names and allowed users and applications to filter legitimate executions
// References:
//   - https://www.zscaler.com/blogs/security-research/onenote-growing-threat-malware-distribution
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_decode_gzip.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "GZipStream" and ProcessCommandLine contains "::Decompress"
